{"availability":"available","full":"avilum/minrlm","name":"minrlm","description":"Replace LLMs reasoning with code execution to solve real-world tasks.","category":"Productivity","language":"Python","stars":81,"forks":6,"created":"2026-01-31T13:26:42Z","updated":"2026-06-11T09:45:05Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://avilum.github.io/minrlm/","topics":["recursive-language-models","rlm","token-optimization"],"demo":"https://avilum.github.io/minrlm/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-13T04:14:48.169Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-13T04:14:48.169Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-13T04:14:48.169Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T18:00:53.639Z","stars":81,"forks":6},{"at":"2026-10-13T04:14:48.169Z","stars":81,"forks":6}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The CLI — the LLM writes Python, a REPL runs it, the answer comes back. The Visualizer — see minRLM and a vanilla LLM run the same task, side-by-side, on any benchmark.","The idea is small and not new: instead of forcing one giant prompt through the model, let it generate code → execute → refine → repeat. The model doesn't change, the training doesn't change, the data doesn't change. The control loop does.","This repo is a minimal, reproducible take on that idea, plus a benchmark — RLM-Bench — that you can run against your own RLM."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/avilum/minrlm/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"38d47bd33d84c51058a18a0b4432652591579c0a5b1cb5349afe4b28b8ea82b7","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T18:00:53.777Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T18:00:53.777Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The CLI — the LLM writes Python, a REPL runs it, the answer comes back. The Visualizer — see minRLM and a vanilla LLM run the same task, side-by-side, on any benchmark.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/avilum/minrlm/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"38d47bd33d84c51058a18a0b4